<title>HONG KONG: Yoshiya year net loss HK$235.88 mln.</title>
<headline>Yoshiya year net loss HK$235.88 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended July 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   122.16 loss vs 9.61 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  216.67 loss vs 2.28 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    235.88 loss vs 18.55 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		     280.92	vs 581.62</p>
<p>    Company name		 Yoshiya International Corp Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Yoshiya International is a property group.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on write-down of certain fixed assets to their estimated recoverable amounts upon cessation of the operations of certain subsidiaries, disposal of fixed assets, write-off of compensation receivable, provision for the group's net assets attributable to the Rayman Group as at July 31, 1995, provision for the amount advanced to Rayman during the year, goodwill previously written off against reserves and bank loans of Rayman assumed by the company.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
